.SH Operators (NORMAL / VISUAL)
\f[CR]d\f[R] (delete), \f[CR]c\f[R] (change), \f[CR]y\f[R] (yank),
\f[CR]>\f[R] \f[CR]<\f[R] (indent / outdent).
.PP
Operator + motion or text object:
.IP
.EX
diw      delete inner word
ci(      change inside parens
ya\[dq]      yank around double\-quoted string
d$       delete to end of line
y2j      yank current + 2 lines below
.EE
.PP
Text objects: \f[CR]iw\f[R] \f[CR]aw\f[R] \f[CR]iW\f[R] \f[CR]aW\f[R]
\f[CR]i(\f[R] \f[CR]a(\f[R] \f[CR]i[\f[R] \f[CR]a[\f[R] \f[CR]i{\f[R]
\f[CR]a{\f[R] \f[CR]i\[dq]\f[R] \f[CR]a\[dq]\f[R] \f[CR]i\[aq]\f[R]
\f[CR]a\[aq]\f[R] \f[CR]i\[ga]\f[R] \f[CR]a\[ga]\f[R].
.PP
Word objects follow Vim semantics: a run of whitespace counts as a word,
so \f[CR]iw\f[R] on a blank selects the blank run; \f[CR]aw\f[R] selects
the word plus trailing blanks (leading blanks if none follow), or \[em]
when the cursor is on whitespace \[em] the blanks plus the following
word.
